Package: secubox-rpi-dsi
Architecture: arm64
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         python3,
         dkms,
         linux-source-6.12,
         linux-headers-arm64,
         patch,
         xz-utils,
         make,
         gcc,
         raspi-firmware,
         initramfs-tools,
         util-linux
Description: SecuBox - official Raspberry Pi 7" DSI touchscreen on the Debian kernel
 OPTIONAL package, for a Raspberry Pi 4 / 400 fitted with the official 7"
 DSI display only. Never pulled by a meta-package or a default image.
 .
 Builds by DKMS, for every installed kernel, patched vc4, tc358762,
 panel-simple and edt-ft5x06 modules from the matching linux-source
 tarball, and installs the secubox-dsi-7inch overlay through
 /etc/default/raspi-firmware-custom (config.txt is never edited).
 Pins ROOTPART in /etc/default/raspi-firmware so raspi-firmware never
 writes root=/dev/mmcblk0p2 into cmdline.txt.
 .
 On any other hardware the postinst does nothing and says so.
